Time and Space Complexity:
Time Complexity:

Iterative Approach: The number of subsets of an array of size n is 2^n. In the worst case, we are generating all subsets, so the time complexity is O(2^n).
Backtracking Approach: Similarly, the time complexity for backtracking is O(2^n) because we are generating all subsets recursively.
Space Complexity:
Iterative Approach: The space complexity is O(2^n), as we store all subsets.
Backtracking Approach: The space complexity is also O(2^n) for storing the subsets in the result. Additionally, the recursion stack takes O(n) space, so the total space complexity is O(2^n + n).

